Repository: /home/devuser/workspace/wt/solid-pod-rs-parity-rescue (Rust workspace, Solid pod server). Branch fix/parity-rescue, to be merged into local main (7718095).
Review ONLY the diff `git diff main...fix/parity-rescue` (run it yourself; read surrounding source as needed). Read-only: do not edit, build or run tests.
Context: this branch recovers uncommitted JSS 0.0.224 parity work (N3 Patch rewrite in crates/solid-pod-rs/src/n3_patch.rs and ldp.rs, a striped per-resource write lock `lock_resource` / `mint_and_lock_target` in crates/solid-pod-rs-server/src/lib.rs, If-Match/If-None-Match on writes, named-pod ACL provisioning `named_pod_acls`, `acl_targets_as_paths` for patched ACLs, Turtle fallback when seeding a PATCH) and reconciles it with main's 3 Nov external-review repairs: malformed-ACL denial and condition preservation in crates/solid-pod-rs/src/wac/parser.rs (main's parser kept; repeated predicates now accumulate via add_ids), proposed_acl_keeps_caller_control (now evaluated under text/turtle, the stored type), canonical payment store, pod export/provenance bound to did:nostr owner, mirror isolation.
Report format: a numbered list of findings, each with severity (critical/high/medium/low), file:line, a concrete failure scenario, and a suggested fix. Mark each finding CONFIRMED (you traced the code path) or SUSPECTED. No praise, no summary of what is fine beyond one line. If there are no findings at a severity, say so.
Role: senior Rust code reviewer. Focus: correctness of the lock (held across read, precondition check and write on every write path; never two stripes held at once by one handler, including via callees; no await-holding deadlock with PAYMENT_STATE_LOCK), N3 patch semantics and regressions vs the old apply_n3_patch callers, N-Triples reader strictness breaking previously-stored bodies, error mapping (PodError::Conflict), API/semver impact of public additions, test quality (do the tests actually prove what they claim), rustdoc accuracy.
